    {
      "type": "content",
      "key": "uitleg",
      "input": false,
      "tableView": false,
      "html": "<h3>Taak data in a form</h3><p>The same mechanism with the taak as its source: <code>taak.naam</code>, <code>taak.groep.naam</code>, <code>ZAC_opmaakDatum(taak.fataledatum)</code>. These properties are read straight off the task itself, so there is no copy that can go stale.</p><p>Both <code>zaak</code> and <code>taak</code> are in the context of every form, so a property that exists on both is whichever one you name. The last row names the taak where the zaak was meant, and renders as empty without complaint.</p><p>Every other row is wrapped in <code>ZAC_opmaakLegeWaarde</code>, so both behaviours are on screen at once: without it an empty property renders as nothing, with it as a dash. It is the same <code>empty</code> pipe the rest of ZAC uses, so a dash here means the same as a dash in the zaak screen.</p>"
    },
